      "side": 1,
      "message": "Trying to think through how this will show up in traces and dashboards, I don\u0027t think we should record the same slice name twice in a row when a compilation is required. Doing so could drag down average duration metrics on dashboards, and confuse engineers looking at traces.\n\nTo preserve parity with how this slice is currently _interpreted_, you could potentially wrap both of these call site blocks with an outer `{ }` block (e.g. wrap lines 564 through 591, inclusive), and place a single `TRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS(\"skia.shaders\", \"CreateGraphicsPipeline\");` at the top?\n\nYou could then augment this by adding a second slice (with a different name like e.g. `CompileGraphicsPipeline` or `CreateGraphicsPipeline-CacheMiss` (IDK)) around just the second call to `vkCreateGraphicsPipelines` to create a nested slice that indicates that this pipeline actually required compilation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 565,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 565,
        "endChar": 67
      },
